                ORDER GRANTING APPEARANCE PRO HAC VICE

      THIS MATTER comes before hearing examiners Patrick Schaefer and Keven Gedko

upon the New Mexico Large Customer Group’s (“NMLCG”) Motion for Admission of

Richard A. Arnett and Thorvald A. Nelson to Appear Pro Hac Vice for NMLCG in this

proceeding in association with local counsels, D. Austin Rueschhoff and Austin W. Jensen,

filed pursuant to 1.2.2.9(E) NMAC on June 25, 2026.

      FINDINGS AND CONCLUSIONS:

      1.     The Declaration and Registration Certificate of Richard A. Arnett attached to

the Motion show that he is a member in good standing of the Bars of Colorado and Texas and

has complied with Rule 24-106 NMRA by filing the requisite Registration Certificate of Non-

Admitted Lawyer with the State Bar of New Mexico.

      2.     The Declaration and Registration Certificate of Thorvald A. Nelson attached to

the Motion show that he is a member in good standing of the Bars of Colorado, Montana,

Nevada, and Wyoming and has complied with Rule 24-106 NMRA by filing the requisite

Registration Certificate of Non-Admitted Lawyer with the State Bar of New Mexico.

      3.     The Motion is unopposed.
                  BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION
Order Granting Appearance Pro Hac Vice                       Docket No. 25-00079-UT


       IT IS THEREFORE ORDERED:

       NMLCG’s Motion is GRANTED. Richard A. Arnett and Thorvald A. Nelson are

admitted to appear in this proceeding pro hac vice in association with local counsels, D. Austin

Rueschhoff and Austin W. Jensen.


       ISSUED under the Seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico this 29th day of

June, 2026.

               NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION




                                Keven Gedko
                                Hearing Examiner



                                ________________________
                                Patrick Schaefer
                                Hearing Examiner




